}
```

The issue is: when `pOut_buf_cur >= pOut_buf_end`, it returns `TINFL_STATUS_HAS_MORE_OUTPUT` with state 53. The `counter` is saved (after the `counter--`). When the function is called again, it resumes at `case 53:` which is inside the `while (counter--)` loop. But the `counter--` has already been applied, so when resuming, it will check `counter--` again, which means it will skip one byte.

